<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S9.T6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table A6</span>: </span><span id="S9.T6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Ablation study on routing strategies using the UnAV100 dataset.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S9.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S9.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S9.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation on routing strategies.</span>
We ablate on having the structure of temporal and MM routing in our proposed network structure as shown in Table <a href="#S9.T6" title="Table A6 ‣ 9 Additional Experiments ‣ Echoes Over Time: Unlocking Length Generalization in Video-to-Audio Generation Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A6</span></a>. We observe that the model with a temporal routing mechanism could improve DeSync scores, which are related to temporal synchronization between audio and visual modalities.</p>
</div>
